{"title":"2019 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Math-X_(First_fully_understand_the_problem!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Math-X (First fully understand the problem!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_Explained\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution Explained</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_ANALYSIS!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (CREATIVE ANALYSIS!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_The_Power_of_Logic(1_to_25_Full_Solution)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by The Power of Logic(1 to 25 Full Solution)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The eighth grade class at Lincoln Middle School has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/2/a72f553051fe3bcf42965f99d1a10ac6efed037e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$93$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> students. Each student takes a math class or a foreign language class or both. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/9/aa94edfb9739dcc66dad90f7dd5c148f44a57e2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$70$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> eighth graders taking a math class, and there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/c/b1cb5bdce2d06d2419066a2b55ab01d824217bd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$54$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" /> eighth graders taking a foreign language class. How many eighth graders take <i>only</i> a math class and <i>not</i> a foreign language class?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/5/5a55044cd065d6d32c6ce0dbc5b70fa4ef5ae6f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }16\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }23\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }31\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }39\\qquad\\textbf{(E) }70$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"398\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since each student must take a math class, a foreign language class, or both, all the students who do not take a foreign language class take a math class.  So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/7/967caf09734e5ee05cf3be92ea4f0ef66adec196.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$93 - 54 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 39}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"149\" height=\"30\" /> students take a math class but not a foreign language class. (The fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/9/aa94edfb9739dcc66dad90f7dd5c148f44a57e2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$70$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> students take a math class is irrelevant.)\n</p><p>-hailstone, edited by j314andrews\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of students taking both a math and a foreign language class.\n</p><p>By P-I-E, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/f/53fbc943df221f68f52e2f571ad71329a11d7c4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$70 + 54 - x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"14\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/2/a72f553051fe3bcf42965f99d1a10ac6efed037e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$93$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Solving gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/1/781414e17428cf4aee3d35e6b60665fe13b3e357.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 31$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"51\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>But we want the number of students taking only a math class,\n</p><p>which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/b/f3bc42fd7e1da2d04b66f911edc9dae9d17ee398.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$70 - 31 = 39$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"100\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/f/ddf39f131a961d02ea84eec3cfb59bb80195f3b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 39}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"65\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>~phoenixfire\n</p>\n<dl><dd>):):):):):)</dd></dl>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/c/04c721414f6dba2e7621ef18a52dfe2d87b18112.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$70 + 54 = 124$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"110\" height=\"14\" /> people taking classes. However, we over-counted the number of people who take both classes. If we subtract the original amount of people who take classes we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/6/296fac336caaa4265aa24b6ecbc408a348ad7e0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> people took the two classes. To find the amount of people who took only math class, we subtract the people who didn't take only one math class, so we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/5/a953139fa8e902788f2fa559ed59c35378d4f87e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$70 - 31 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)} \\, 39}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"147\" height=\"30\" />. \n</p><p>-fath2012\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/f/b2f07041effb65f84f21bac99d7f4f0c292c18b7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw(circle((-0.5,0),1)); draw(circle((0.5,0),1)); label(&quot;$\\huge{x}$&quot;, (0, 0)); label(&quot;$70-x$&quot;, (-1, 0)); label(&quot;$54-x$&quot;, (1, 0)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"168\" />\n</p><p>We know that the sum of all three areas is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/2/a72f553051fe3bcf42965f99d1a10ac6efed037e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$93$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />\nSo, we have: \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/7/957e6020bc84fcd4dc822b45f5c0c0e9bbc10fb8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[93 = 70-x+x+54-x\\]\" width=\"198\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/9/2892d379e250aab5337706f0020b1b6dc440370a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[93 = 70+54-x\\]\" width=\"133\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/5/5e5f58eb7dacfae6741cac7101024975dc4727f6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[93 = 124 - x\\]\" width=\"101\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/7/187c88af85602ec8c5e334c05cc4379424a4711f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-31=-x\\]\" width=\"79\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/0/7c0ebdc4866f572d386222d480abe1b80674c659.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x=31\\]\" width=\"51\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>We are looking for the number of students in only math. This is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/d/9dd33731db730503552206539498c16787e456e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$70-x$\" width=\"50\" height=\"12\" />. Substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/6/296fac336caaa4265aa24b6ecbc408a348ad7e0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/d/1fd830d446f41bf02b20f14671ad1532f36f2518.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{39}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>-mathnerdnair\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_Math-X_.28First_fully_understand_the_problem.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Math-X_(First_fully_understand_the_problem!!!)\">Video Solution by Math-X (First fully understand the problem!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Math-X (First fully understand the problem!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/IgpayYB48C4?si=hwYx8EF3iCm50Ms8&amp;t=3557\">https://youtu.be/IgpayYB48C4?si=hwYx8EF3iCm50Ms8&amp;t=3557</a> \n</p><p>~Math-X\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_Explained\">Solution Explained</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution Explained\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/gOZOCFNXMhE\">https://youtu.be/gOZOCFNXMhE</a> ~ The Learning Royal\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Associated video - <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=onPaMTO3dSA\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=onPaMTO3dSA</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Solution detailing how to solve the problem: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Kanl4ni2y0o&amp;list=PLbhMrFqoXXwmwbk2CWeYOYPRbGtmdPUhL&amp;index=12\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Kanl4ni2y0o&amp;list=PLbhMrFqoXXwmwbk2CWeYOYPRbGtmdPUhL&amp;index=12</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/4E8I-NJYAJY\">https://youtu.be/4E8I-NJYAJY</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28CREATIVE_ANALYSIS.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_ANALYSIS!!!)\">Video Solution (CREATIVE ANALYSIS!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (CREATIVE ANALYSIS!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/2K2ZUw-l1ek\">https://youtu.be/2K2ZUw-l1ek</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_The_Power_of_Logic.281_to_25_Full_Solution.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_The_Power_of_Logic(1_to_25_Full_Solution)\">Video Solution by The Power of Logic(1 to 25 Full Solution)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by The Power of Logic(1 to 25 Full Solution)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Xm4ZGND9WoY\">https://youtu.be/Xm4ZGND9WoY</a>\n</p><p>~Hayabusa1\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; wi